class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Ashley County has 75 years on record since 1951, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, April to May ran 173% of normal and November to December just 50%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 41% and June to July at 73%, and grid 16052 shows a preliminary August to September 2026 estimate of 31.4.</p>"}
